+/*
+ * One HFI decoder session per client, the way Linux vdec.c drives a 4xx core: session init, input size,
+ * core 1, output configuration, buffer counts, internal buffers, LOAD_RESOURCES, START; the first input
+ * buffers until SEQUENCE_CHANGED reports the stream; then the output side ("capture setup"): split mode
+ * with linear NV12 frames on OUTPUT2 for the client and UBWC NV12 reference (DPB) buffers on OUTPUT,
+ * kept by the driver (v4 offers linear NV12 only on OUTPUT2: hfi_platform_v4.c), CONTINUE, every DPB and
+ * output buffer queued (dynamic buffer mode). EBD frees an input buffer, FBD on stream 1 is a decoded
+ * picture, on stream 0 a DPB buffer back (queued again).
+ */
